<title>BRAZIL: Brazil gov't rejects soy export tax proposal.</title>
<headline>Brazil gov't rejects soy export tax proposal.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian government's Foreign Trade Chamber has rejected a proposal from domestic vegetable oil producers who wanted a new tax for soybean exports, a trade official said.</p>
<p>Frederico Alvarez, the chamber's executive secretary, said the proposal for a 3.5 percent tax on soybean exports from the Brazilian Vegetable Oil Industry Association (Abiove) had been rejected.</p>
<p>Abiove had wanted the government to impose the tax to slow down shipments overseas of Brazilian soybeans.</p>
<p>(( -- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358))</p>
